{% set c = host.value.config ?? {} %}
<section class="card" aria-labelledby="si-h">
<h2 id="si-h">SMTP identity</h2>
<p>How this server introduces itself to other mail servers. Receivers check that these names, the IP address and its reverse DNS agree.</p>
<dl class="rows">
<dt>Mail host name (EHLO, PTR)</dt><dd><code>{{ c.POSTFIX_MYHOSTNAME ?? '?' }}</code> — Postfix greets other servers with this name; the PTR of the IP must be this name, and its A record must be this IP.</dd>
<dt>Public IPv4</dt><dd><code>{{ c.SMARTHOST_PUBLIC_IPV4 ?? '?' }}</code> — the sending address. catto-mail sends over IPv4 only.</dd>
<dt>Bounce domain</dt><dd><code>{{ c.SMARTHOST_BOUNCE_DOMAIN ?? '?' }}</code> — the envelope sender of every message (<code>bounce+&lt;token&gt;@…</code>); bounces and complaints return here. Its MX must point at the mail host name.</dd>
<dt>Sign-in mail sender</dt><dd><code>{{ c.APP_MAIL_FROM ?? '?' }}</code> — its domain needs a DKIM key too.</dd>
</dl>
<p>Change them in <code>infra/.env</code> as for the web identity. The PTR is set at your VPS provider, not in your DNS zone.</p>
</section>
